zark-gnome-app (1.1.1-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Fixes from the first eli checklist: the launcher keeps python3 -I in
    the package; a redraw keeps the page's scroll and open months; the
    run's percentage comes from bytes only and is complete once the data
    is sent; backup points in local time; a drive mounted for browsing
    offers Open and Unmount and no Back Up.

 -- Juanmi Taboada <juanmi@juanmitaboada.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:41:13 +0100

zark-gnome-app (1.1-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Operations (A2): every action of the design runs one zark command
    through pkexec under its own polkit action, in an embedded terminal;
    Stop, Close and Quit during a run ask first; logout and suspend are
    inhibited while the app's run lasts. Depends on pkexec and
    gir1.2-vte-3.91.

 -- Juanmi Taboada <juanmi@juanmitaboada.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:00:00 +0100

zark-gnome-app (1.0-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * First version (A1): the state of zark's backups, read-only, from the
    status files of the installed zark 2.3.0 or later.

